# Vercel + TrimDrop

## “403 Forbidden” (or 401) inside the Vercel **deployment preview** panel
That iframe often hits a **protected preview URL** (`*-frost-povs-projects.vercel.app`). Those can return **401** and set **`X-Frame-Options: DENY`**, so the embedded preview looks blocked even when the deploy succeeded.

**Test the real site** with the production domain: **`https://trimdrop-ke.vercel.app`** (or whatever you set as Production).

To show previews without auth: **Project → Settings → Deployment Protection** → adjust **Vercel Authentication** / preview protection (team policy).

## Static entry
- **`index.html`** is the main page at **`/`**.
- **`vercel.json`** rewrites **`/trimdrop.html` → `/`** for old links.
